 {"clause_id": "c008",
  "issues": [
   {"issue": "Rights turn on whether a well is \"capable of producing in paying quantities\", a phrase left undefined and notoriously contestable, and the 80/40-acre \"circle\" is described by area without any stated radius or survey method. Both are terms whose boundary a court would have to fix.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.44},
   {"issue": "The Exhibit \"D\" form of assignment leaves the acreage of the circle blank, so the instrument that actually conveys the rights does not carry forward the 80/40-acre measure fixed here. The two must be reconciled to know what is conveyed.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27}
  ]},
 {"clause_id": "c009",
  "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Lease burdens\" ends with the catch-all \"and other similar burdens on production\" after an enumeration of royalty, overriding royalty and production payment, leaving its reach open to an ejusdem generis argument. Whether items such as net profits interests fall inside is unresolved.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26},
