 {"clause_id": "c030",
  "issues": [
   {"issue": "The royalty is on \"gross proceeds received from the sale of oil and/or gas produced from wells drilled hereunder without deductions of any kind\", which does not say at what point of sale proceeds are measured or whether post-production costs may be borne by the royalty. \"Gross proceeds ... without deductions\" is exactly the phrase such disputes turn on.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.44},
   {"issue": "Section 4(A) allows \"no deductions of any kind\", but the Exhibit \"D\" assignment form reserves the same royalty \"without deductions of any kind, except that Assignor shall bear its proportionate part of any severance tax\". The instrument that implements the reservation contradicts the reservation itself.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.36}
  ]},
 {"clause_id": "c031",
  "issues": [
   {"issue": "The notice duty is triggered when a well is not capable of producing in paying quantities or \"ceases production\", a phrase with no duration or materiality qualifier, so any temporary interruption may trip it. Whether a brief cessation counts is a construction question.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
   {"issue": "Section 5(A) requires notice and abandonment when a well \"ceases production\", while Section 7(A) contemplates a capable well simply being shut in for 45 days or longer against a shut-in royalty. The same well can fall under both regimes with opposite consequences.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
  ]},
 {"clause_id": "c032",
  "issues": [
   {"issue": "Termination follows if Farmee fails to give Farmor \"a reasonable opportunity to consider its options\", a standard stated without any measure even though Section 5(A) already prescribes exact 30-day and 48-hour windows. What more \"reasonable opportunity\" requires is undefined.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
   {"issue": "This subsection terminates the Agreement only \"as to the Unearned Farmout Lands\", yet Section 13(A) lists 5(B) among the provisions by which \"This Farmout Agreement terminates\". The scope of a 5(B) termination is inconsistent between the two.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.32}
  ]},
 {"clause_id": "c033",
  "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause requires Farmee to assign \"any Operating Rights Earned by Farmor and earned by Farmee\", a garbled formula that attributes the same earned rights to both parties. Reimbursement at \"estimated salvage value ... less estimated plugging costs\" also leaves unsaid who makes the estimates.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.35},
   {"issue": "Section 6 by its terms governs only a takeover \"under the terms and conditions of Section 5\", but Section 3(F) invokes Section 6 for a takeover on default of wells that have not satisfied the earning requirements. The default takeover has no complete mechanic of its own.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.33}
  ]},
 {"clause_id": "c034",
  "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause charges a shut-in royalty \"per well per year, prorated on a monthly basis\" yet makes it \"due and payable by the last day of each month any such well is shut-in\", leaving annual versus monthly accrual unclear. The trigger \"shut in for any reason\" is also unqualified.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
   {"issue": "Section 7(A) applies to any capable well \"whether or not such well has already produced\", while Section 2(H) defines a \"shut-in well\" as one \"that has previously produced and is still capable of producing in commercial quantities\". The class of wells owing shut-in royalty differs between the two.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.36}
  ]},
 {"clause_id": "c035",
  "issues": [
   {"issue": "The notice duty is qualified by \"When possible\", a self-judging condition that supplies no test for when advance notice may be omitted. The obligation is effectively unmeasurable as drafted.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
  ]},
 {"clause_id": "c036",
  "issues": [
   {"issue": "The indemnity covers losses \"of any kind or character incurred by Farmor and arising out of, in connection with, or resulting from the operations, actions or omissions of Farmee\" without saying whether it reaches losses caused by Farmor's own negligence. The bracketed enumeration also sits against the words \"including but not limited to\", leaving the catch-all's reach open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.34},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
  ]},
 {"clause_id": "c037",
  "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.14},
   {"issue": "Farmee must keep the Farmout Lands \"free and clear from all liens\", yet the Exhibit \"D\" assignment gives Assignor \"a lien on all future production and proceeds\" for unpaid overriding royalty and Section 15(D) contemplates liens created with Farmor's consent. The absolute prohibition cannot be read literally against those provisions.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
 {"clause_id": "c038",
  "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Farmor does not warrant title, either express or implied\" is grammatically incoherent — the adjectives modify nothing — and the sentence never says whether statutory or after-acquired-title warranties are also disclaimed. A court would have to supply the intended disclaimer.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
  ]},
 {"clause_id": "c039",
  "issues": [
   {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.13},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.11}
  ]},
 {"clause_id": "c040",
  "issues": [
   {"issue": "The clause says notices \"shall be given as follows\" and then supplies only addresses, phone and fax numbers, without specifying an acceptable method of delivery or when notice is deemed received. Whether a fax or telephone call is effective notice is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24},
   {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
  ]}
]}

